@startuml datarouter_dynamic_design

participant "DatarouterMessageClientImpl\n(client process)" as Client
participant "MessagePassingServer\ndispatch thread" as Dispatch
participant "SocketServer" as SS
participant "DataRouter" as DR
participant "MessagePassingServer\nworker thread" as Worker
participant "SharedMemoryReader" as SMR
participant "LogParser\n(per session)" as LP
participant "DltLogServer" as DLS

== Session establishment ==

Client -> Dispatch : kConnect(appid, uid, random_part)\n[client PID from QNX transport, not message field]
note over Dispatch
  Dispatch thread holds mutex_.
  Cross-checks transport PID against SharedData::producer_pid.
  Rejects if mismatch (security check).
end note
Dispatch -> SS : CreateMessagePassingSession(pid, conn, handle)
SS -> DR : NewSourceSession(pid, ...)
DR -> DR : create SourceSession\n(allocates LogParser + SharedMemoryReader;\nadds to sources_ under subscriber_mutex_)
DR --> SS : MessagingSessionPtr
SS --> Dispatch : ISession
Dispatch --> Client : ConnectResponse

== Log data transfer (per flush) ==

note over Client
  Application thread writes to shared memory
  via SharedMemoryWriter::AllocAndWrite()
  without contacting the daemon.
end note

Worker -> Client : kAcquireRequest\n(daemon requests buffer switch)
Client -> Dispatch : kAcquireResponse(ReadAcquireResult)\n(client called SharedMemoryWriter::ReadAcquire())
Dispatch -> Worker : store data_acquired;\nenqueue pid in work_queue_\n(under mutex_; signal worker_cond_)

note over Worker, SMR
  Tick() runs two phases.
  The ReadAcquireResult received above
  is stored in command_data_.data_acquired.
end note

note over Worker, SMR
  Phase 1: TryFinalizeAcquisition()
end note
Worker -> SMR : IsBlockReleasedByWriters(block_count)\n— polls until number_of_writers==0\n  AND written_index==acquired_index\n— acquire fence on true
SMR --> Worker : gate cleared
Worker -> SMR : NotifyAcquisitionSetReader(acquire_result)\n— sets up reader for acquired buffer

note over Worker, SMR
  Phase 2: ProcessAndRouteLogMessages()
end note
Worker -> SMR : Read(on_new_type, on_new_record)\n— AlternatingReadOnlyReader::CreateLinearReader()\n— iterate entries; invoke callbacks per entry
note right of SMR
  Two callbacks per Read():
  on_new_type → parser_->AddIncomingType()
  on_new_record → parser_->ParseSharedMemoryRecord()
  (skipped when quota_overlimit_detected)
end note

Worker -> LP : on_new_record: ParseSharedMemoryRecord(record)\n— per-type handlers dispatch\n  to DltLogServer via IOutput
alt unknown TypeIdentifier
  LP -> LP : silently drop entry\n(not in index_parser_map_)
else known TypeIdentifier
  LP -> DLS : SendVerbose() or SendNonVerbose()\n(via registered per-type handler)
  DLS -> DLS : apply context filters (config_mutex_)
  DLS -> DLS : forward to DLT subsystem\n(UDP multicast / file)
end

== Session teardown — clean disconnect and crash ==

note over Client, Dispatch
  QNX message-passing channel fires peer-close event.
  Clean disconnect: client already called DetachWriter()
  (SharedData::writer_detached = true).
  Crash: writer_detached = false.
  Both paths are handled identically.
end note

Dispatch -> Dispatch : disconnect_callback\n— to_force_finish = true\n— EnqueueForDeleteWhileLocked(true):\n  to_delete = true, closed_by_peer = true

Worker -> Worker : closed_by_peer == true\n→ NotifyClosedByPeer()\n→ SourceSession::OnClosedByPeer():\n  command_detach_on_closed = true

Worker -> SMR : ReadDetached(on_new_type, on_new_record)\n(drains remaining records if writer_detached;\nsets detach_on_closed_processed = true)

Worker -> Worker : to_force_finish == true\n→ pid_session_map_.extract(pid)\n→ SourceSession destructor\n  (unmaps shared memory, frees LogParser)

note over Worker
  Stale-session watchdog:
  ticks_without_write incremented each tick.
  Exceeding threshold → schedule for teardown
  (guards against crash before channel-close propagates).
end note

@enduml
